# Commits for `git blame` to skip, such as bulk reformatting, so blame shows
# the commit that last really changed each line instead. `just` sets
# `blame.ignoreRevsFile` to this file (scripts/git-config-setup.sh); without
# `just`, run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`. GitHub's
# blame view reads it too.
#
# Format: one full 40-character commit hash per line. Blank lines and lines
# starting with `#` are ignored, so put a comment above each hash saying what
# the commit was. Use the commit's hash on `master`: squash merges give it a
# new one, so add it once the PR has merged.

